\section{Proposed study}
We will re-train ViT-B/16 and DeiT-B under a unified protocol: ImageNet-1K only pre-training, 224×224 resolution, 300 epochs, AdamW optimizer, standard data augmentation (random resized cropping, horizontal flip, MixUp, CutMix). Both models will be evaluated in three configurations: (i) non-distilled baseline, (ii) DeiT-style distillation with a ConvNet teacher (e.g., RegNetY-8GF), and (iii) a ViT counterpart trained with the same distillation pipeline to assess whether the gains are attributable to the architecture or the distillation token. Each configuration will be run with five different random seeds; we will report mean top-1 accuracy and 95 \% confidence intervals. Additionally, we will ablate the number of pre-training epochs to examine data-efficiency: whether DeiT matches or exceeds ViT accuracy with fewer epochs while keeping all other factors equal. Limitations include the reliance on a single teacher architecture for distillation, the exclusion of external-data pre-training regimes (e.g., JFT-300M) from the primary comparison, and the potential sensitivity to optimizer hyper-parameters that were not exhaustively explored in the source papers.
\subsection{Controls required by the evidence}
\begin{itemize}
\item Treat a cited copy of a baseline as the original paper's result, not as new evidence; re-run baselines under the shared protocol.
\item Match and report image resolution before attributing an outcome difference to the method.
\end{itemize}
